{"kind":"request","text":"Join parity: joining through MCP does what Start and the CLI do\n\nHugh, 9 November 2026: the Start page and joining through MCP behave the same way. This answers the checker's request 34c4b1a1.\n\nA person or an agent who joins a room through the MCP join tool ends up with the same membership as one who joins through the Start page or `dap join`: the same invites accepted, the same key and custody, the same recorded controller facts, the same scope and incarnation checks, and the same directory and inbox verification. The check mode (`--check` on the CLI) has an MCP equivalent.\n\nWork:\n1. Inventory first, read-only. For each join mode that Start or the CLI supports today (person join, tagged agent-key join or enrolment, check), say whether MCP join supports it on current main, with file and line. Report the inventory on this request before any source edit.\n2. Close every gap with one shared parser and one shared judge for invites, used by all three surfaces. Do not add a second copy. Delete any legacy invite parser that only MCP uses.\n3. docs/mcp.md and the join documentation say that the three surfaces are equal, and name any limit that stays.\n\nWitnesses: one invite joined through the CLI and one through MCP record the same membership facts for the same kind of member, for a person and for a tagged agent key. MCP check reports the same answer as CLI check for a valid invite and for a refused one.\n\nOrder: the inventory (item 1) may run as filler at the end of phase 1 of afdebb86. Items 2 and 3 are phase 3 work, after C1 and M1a resume. Checker review of each exact head; one gate at the final head; no builder deployment. Hosted MCP stays closed on the Workers, so the witnesses use the local MCP server.","body":{"conditions":"Read-only join inventory reported first; then one shared invite parser and judge for Start, CLI and MCP; witnesses for person and tagged agent-key join and for check; docs say the surfaces are equal. Checker review per exact head; one gate at the final head; no builder deployment.","target_head":"c9583a00b3d7ee99464585878780e1d51fae4208","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}